See Common Known Issues 1).

3.4 Intel Sapphire Rapids
-------------------------

Sapphire Rapids is the codename for Intel 4th Gen Xeon Scalable Processor, and it is a part of
the Eagle Stream server platform.

3.4.1 Validated Board Info
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This BSP is only validated in the following environment. If you use this BSP
in a different environment it may have some issues.

[BIOS Info]
  Vendor: Intel Corporation
  Version: EGSDCRB1.SYS.9409.P01.2211280753
  Release Date: 11/28/2022

[Processor Info]
  CPU family      : 6
  Model           : 143
  Model name      : Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8468H
  Stepping        : 6
  Microcode       : 0xab000161

[Board Info]
  Intel Archer City Modular

3.4.2 Supported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	o Bus
		+ PCI-Express
		+ SMBus:
			+ SMBus [0c05]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:1bc9] (rev 11)

	o Network
		+ Intel Gigabit Ethernet:
			+ Ethernet controller [0200]: Intel Corporation I210 Gigabit Network Connection [8086:1533] (rev 03)

	o USB
		+ USB 3.0 XHCI controller:
			+ USB controller [0c03]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:1bcd] (rev 11)

	o Storage
		+ SATA:
			+ SATA controller [0106]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:1ba2] (rev 11)

	o Multimedia
		+ Graphics:
			+ VGA compatible controller [0300]: ASPEED Technology, Inc. ASPEED Graphics Family [1a03:2000] (rev 52)

	o Power Management
		+ Suspend to IDLE: ACPI S0
		+ Suspend to DISK: ACPI S4
		+ CPU Freq: ACPI P-state
		+ CPU Idle: ACPI C-state

	o Misc Devices
		+ Input device:
			+ USB mouse & keyboard
		+ UART

	o TPM2.0
		+ IFX0785:00: 2.0 TPM (device-id 0x1B, rev-id 22)

	o Intel Data Streaming Accelerators
		+ System peripheral [0880]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:0b25]
		+ System peripheral [0880]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:0cfe]

	o Intel QuickAssist Technology (QAT)
		+ Co-processor [0b40]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:4940] (rev 40)

	o Intel Optane Persistent Memory 300 series (Crow Pass)

3.4.3 Unsupported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following feature is not supported and not validated.

  x Intel Software Guard Extensions (SGX)
  x Audio device [0403]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:1bc8]

There is no external interface for audio device on server platform. So this feature
is not validated.

3.4.4 Notes
~~~~~~~~~~~
1) In order to support QAT device on Sapphire Rapids, you need to enable feature/intel-qat
and set the following PREFERRED_PROVIDER before building.

  PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/qat = "qat20"
  PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/lib32-qat = "qat20"
or
  PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/qat = "qatlib"
  PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/lib32-qat = "qatlib"

Please read templates/feature/intel-qat/README first.

2) Default console serial port is ttyS0 at I/O 0x3f8.

3.5 Intel Harcuvar(Denverton-NS)
--------------------------------

Harcuvar belongs to Denverton SoC Product Family, with support of DDR4, 4x SFP+
and QAT.

3.5.1 Validated Board Info
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This BSP is only validated in the following environment. If you use this BSP
in a different environment it may possibly have some issues.

[BIOS info]
	BIOS Version: HAVLCRB1.X64.0015.D62.1708310404

[Processor info]
	Codename	: Denverton-NS
	vendor_id       : GenuineIntel
	Core		: 16
	ID		: 0x506F1
	Stepping	: 1
	Microcode Rev	: 0x10

[Board info]
	Platform: Intel Harcuvar

3.5.2 Supported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following BSP features are validated and supported.

	o Bus
		+ PCI-Express
		+ SMBus:
			+ Intel Corporation Atom Processor C3000 Series SMBus controller [8086:19df] (rev 10)

	o Network
		+ Intel Gigabit Ethernet
			+ Intel Corporation I210 Gigabit Network Connection [8086:1533] (rev 03)
		+ Intel IXGBE Ethernet:
			+ Intel Corporation Ethernet Connection X553 10 GbE SFP+ [8086:15ce] (rev 10)

	o USB
		+ USB 2.0 EHCI controller
		+ USB 3.0 XHCI controller
			+ Intel Corporation Atom Processor C3000 Series USB 3.0 xHCI Controller [8086:19d0] (rev 10) (prog-if 30 [XHCI])

	o Storage
		+ SATA: AHCI SATA controller
			+ Intel Corporation Atom Processor C3000 Series SATA Controller 1 [8086:19c2] (rev 10) (prog-if 01 [AHCI 1.0])
		+ eMMC card:
			+ SD Host controller [0805]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:19db] (rev 01) (prog-if 01)

	o Misc Devices
		+ UART: 8250/16550A compatible serial port
			+ Intel Corporation Atom Processor C3000 Series HSUART Controller [8086:19d8] (rev 10) (prog-if 02 [16550]
		+ Input device
			+ USB mouse & keyboard
		+ Hardware Watchdog
			+ Intel iTCO H/W Watchdog Timer

	o Intel QuickAssist Technology (QAT)
		+ Co-processor [0b40]: Intel Corporation Atom Processor C3000 Series QuickAssist Technology [8086:19e2] (rev 10)

	o Power Management
		+ Suspend to IDLE: ACPI S0
		+ Suspend to DISK: ACPI S4
		+ CPU Freq: ACPI P-state
		+ CPU Idle: ACPI C-state

3.5.3 Unsupported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following features are not supported and not validated.

	x Suspend to Memory (ACPI S3) (Not supported by BIOS)
	x SPI (Hardware Sequencing Flash Status Control register isn't well configured in BIOS, timeout when read/write)

3.5.4 Known Issues
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

When using ACPI S4, kernel cannot exit from hibernation and the terminal hangup without any output. This is due to driver of
VGA controller Millennium G550. If you want to use ACPI S4, change another card or block probing the driver by adding
"modprobe.blacklist=matroxfb_base" to boot parameters.

4. Common Known Issues
======================

1) Engineer Samples of Intel Ethernet Adapter sometimes don't have valid MAC addresses, like

    root@intel-x86-64:~# ifconfig | grep ether
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:00
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:01
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:02
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:03

Before performing network testing, ensure that valid MAC addresses are assigned to each interface.
